# AAP labels: one primary demo label on every object

Every `aap-demo-*` artifact must expose a **single primary label** that uniquely identifies
the demo in the Controller UI, so an operator can filter Job Templates, Workflows, and any
other labelable object down to *this* demo alone — even when dozens of demos share the same
AAP. Secondary labels (e.g. `Preflight`, `Patching`, `Cleanup`) are encouraged for
cross-cutting filters, but they **never replace** the primary label.

## Primary label

1. Define **`demo_label_name`** in `demo_variables.yml.example` (demo identity section —
   see **`artifact--demo-variables.mdc`**). Derive the value from the artifact title or slug
   (e.g. `PoC App Stack Restart`, `Slack Notifications`). It must be **unique across every
   sibling artifact** deployed to the same AAP — the same uniqueness bar as
   `demo_organization_name`.
2. Declare it in `group_vars/all/labels.yml` under `controller_labels`, scoped to the demo
   organization:

   ```yaml
   controller_labels:
     - name: "{{ demo_label_name }}"
       organization: "{{ demo_organization_name }}"
   ```

3. Apply it to **every** CasC object that accepts a `labels:` field. At minimum this means
   every job template and every workflow job template (including infra-gated
   `*_infra.yml` counterparts and the preflight suite). Also apply it to inventories and
   projects when those CasC files set `labels:`.

## Secondary labels

Objects may carry additional labels alongside the primary one:

```yaml
labels:
  - "{{ demo_label_name }}"
  - Preflight
```

- Declare every secondary label in `labels.yml` as well (same organization).
- Common secondary labels: `Preflight` (see **`artifact--preflight-checks.mdc`**),
  functional tags such as `Patching`, `Provisioning`, `Cleanup`.
- A secondary label alone is **not** enough. Filtering the UI by `demo_label_name` must still
  return the object.

## Anti-patterns (do not ship)

```yaml
# WRONG — preflight-only; disappears when filtering by the demo's primary label
labels:
  - Preflight

# WRONG — hardcoded string instead of the shared identity variable
labels:
  - PoC App Stack Restart

# CORRECT
labels:
  - "{{ demo_label_name }}"
  - Preflight
```

## Scope notes

- Labels apply to Controller objects that support them via CasC (`controller_templates`,
  `controller_workflows`, and optionally `controller_inventories` / `controller_projects`).
  Credentials, credential types, execution environments, and organizations do not take
  `labels:` — do not invent a field there.
- Labels are removed with the Organization on cleanup (no direct delete API) — see
  **`artifact--casc-playbooks.mdc`**.

## Checklist

- [ ] `demo_label_name` is set to a unique, human-readable demo title in
      `demo_variables.yml.example`
- [ ] `labels.yml` declares `{{ demo_label_name }}` (and every secondary label used)
- [ ] Every job template and workflow job template lists `"{{ demo_label_name }}"` first in
      `labels:`
- [ ] Preflight job templates and `WF - Preflight Checks` carry both
      `"{{ demo_label_name }}"` and `Preflight` — never `Preflight` alone
- [ ] No CasC object that supports labels ships without the primary demo label
